@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "SMS Consent";
}

<article class="legal-page">
    <h1>TryOutSpot SMS Consent Flow</h1>
    <p><strong>Effective date:</strong> May 8, 2026</p>

    <p>
        TryOutSpot sends transactional SMS messages only to users who provide a mobile phone number
        and explicitly opt in to transactional SMS messages during account signup.
    </p>

    <h2>Public Opt-In Path</h2>
    <p>
        A user can opt in on the public account registration page at
        <a href="/account/register">https://tryoutspot.com/account/register</a>.
        The SMS consent checkbox is unchecked by default. SMS consent is optional and is not required
        to create a TryOutSpot account.
    </p>

    <h2>Consent Checkbox Text</h2>
    <div class="sms-consent-example">
        <input type="checkbox" disabled />
        <span>@TryOutSpotSmsConsent.CheckboxText</span>
    </div>
    <p>
        The registration page also links directly to the
        <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a> and
        <a href="/terms-and-conditions">Terms and Conditions</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Message Types</h2>
    <p>
        Messages may include phone verification codes, account security notices, password reset
        notifications, tryout registration updates, and related account or service alerts.
    </p>

    <h2>Disclosures</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Message frequency varies based on account activity and registrations.</li>
        <li>Message and data rates may apply.</li>
        <li>Reply STOP to opt out.</li>
        <li>Reply HELP for help.</li>
        <li>SMS consent is not a condition of purchasing goods or services.</li>
        <li>Mobile information is not shared with third parties or affiliates for marketing or promotional purposes.</li>
    </ul>
</article>
